<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Copy for :feature:files. Shared chrome copy (Back, Delete, Cancel, Try again, Select all, the
  AppError messages, the twenty feature titles) stays in :core:ui and is referenced from there.

  WORDING BAN (LLM.md §1, §5) — absolute, and a CI grep over strings.xml enforces it. No string below
  makes a performance, security or memory claim, and none carries a percentage figure. Every screen
  here reports BYTES, measured, and says what it could not reach.

  Two rules the competitor breaks and these strings do not:
    * every count goes through a <plurals>. The competitor appends an English "s" and ships
      "Delete <n> videos (12.3MB )" — with a literal trailing space — to all 17 of its locales.
    * a coverage or truncation statement is never omitted. A scan that could not see everything says
      so (docs/system-architecture.md §8.4).
-->
